# Module service providers (bltdreeg-server)

## Rule

Each domain under `app/Modules/V1/{Name}/` **must** have `{Name}ServiceProvider` that owns that module’s registrations. Register every module provider in that app’s `bootstrap/providers.php`.

**Do not** put module-specific `Gate::policy`, container bindings, observers, route loads, or Filament response bindings in `App\Providers\AppServiceProvider`.

`AppServiceProvider` stays for **app-wide** concerns only (e.g. `Gate::before` super-admin, LanguageSwitch, global PermissionRegistrar wiring).

## Pattern (ATS-style)

```
app/Modules/V1/{Name}/
  {Name}ServiceProvider.php
  Filament/…
  Policies/…
  …
```

```php
// bootstrap/providers.php
return [
    AppServiceProvider::class,
    AppPanelProvider::class, // or AdminPanelProvider
    \App\Modules\V1\Auth\AuthServiceProvider::class,
    \App\Modules\V1\Hr\HrServiceProvider::class,
    // …every V1 module
];
```

```php
namespace App\Modules\V1\Hr;

class HrServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function register(): void { /* bindings */ }

    public function boot(): void
    {
        Gate::policy(JobType::class, JobTypePolicy::class);
        // …
    }
}
```

## Applies to

- `tenant-app`
- `central-app`

Shared package policies/observers may stay in `Bltdreeg\Core\Providers\CoreServiceProvider` when they belong to `packages/core`, not to one app module.

### Private file downloads (central-app)

Do **not** add one-off controllers per document type. Instead:

1. Implement `Bltdreeg\Core\Contracts\PrivateStoredFile` on the model
2. Register it in the owning module provider: `PrivateFileRegistry::register($type, Model::class)`
3. Link with `PrivateFileController::temporaryUrl($model)` (signed route `private-files.show`)

## When adding a new module

1. Create `app/Modules/V1/{Name}/{Name}ServiceProvider.php`
2. Move that module’s policies/bindings into it
3. Append the provider class to `bootstrap/providers.php`
4. Do **not** grow `AppServiceProvider` with module code
